{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
<p>Layouts hold the markup that pages share. A layout defines named <code>block</code> sections, and a page <code>extends</code> the layout and fills them in.</p>

{% set layout %}
{% verbatim %}
<title>{% block title %}{{ site.name }}{% endblock %}</title>
<main>
	{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</main>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endset %}
{% apply example(templates: { "layouts/base.kiln": layout }, context: { page: { title: "About us" } }) %}
{% verbatim %}
{% extends "layouts/base" %}

{% block title %}{{ page.title }} | {{ parent() }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
	<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
{% endblock %}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<h2>Pages</h2>

<ul>
	<li><code>extends</code> must be the first tag in the template.</li>
	<li>The name can be any expression, such as <code>layout ?? "layouts/base"</code>.</li>
	<li>Outside blocks, a page can only contain <code>set</code>, <code>props</code>, <code>import</code>, <code>from</code>, <code>macro</code> and comments. Anything else is an error, because it would never be shown.</li>
	<li>Top-level <code>set</code> tags run before the layout renders. The layout and every block can use their variables.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Blocks</h2>

<ul>
	<li>Block names must be unique within a template.</li>
	<li><code>&#123;% endblock title %}</code> may repeat the name. If it does, it must match.</li>
	<li><code>&#123;% block title page.title %}</code> is a short form for a block that holds one expression.</li>
	<li>Layouts can extend other layouts, as deep as you need.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Reusing blocks</h2>

<p><code>parent()</code> outputs the layout's version of the current block. <code>block("name")</code> outputs another block of the current template again, and <code>block("name") is defined</code> checks that it exists.</p>

{% apply highlight("kiln") %}
{% verbatim %}
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ block("title") }}">

{% if block("sidebar") is defined %}
	<aside>{{ block("sidebar") }}</aside>
{% endif %}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>To render one block on its own, such as a fragment for a partial page update, see <a href="/docs/api/rendering/#rendering-one-block"><code>renderBlock</code></a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
